Information about our competitors is included in Part I, Item 1 of this Annual Report on Form 10-K under the
heading “COMPETITION”.
Our business is subject to many factors that could cause our quarterly or annual operating results to fluctuate
and our stock price to be volatile.
Our quarterly and annual operating results have fluctuated in the past and may fluctuate significantly in the
future due to a variety of factors, many of which are outside of our control. Some of the factors that could affect our
quarterly or annual operating results include:
(cid:129) the timing and amount, or cancellation or rescheduling, of orders for our products or services;
(cid:129) our ability to develop, introduce, ship and support new products, services and enhancements, and
manage product and services transitions;
(cid:129) announcements of new product and service introductions and reductions in the price of products and
services offered by our competitors;
(cid:129) our ability to achieve cost reductions;
(cid:129) our ability to obtain sufficient supplies of sole or limited source components for our products;
(cid:129) our ability to achieve and maintain production volumes and quality levels for our products;
(cid:129) our ability to maintain the volume of products and services sold and the mix of distribution channels
through which they are sold;
(cid:129) the loss of any one of our major customers or a significant reduction in orders from those customers;
(cid:129) increased competition, particularly from larger, better capitalized competitors;
(cid:129) fluctuations in demand for our products and services; and
(cid:129) changes in telecommunications and wireless market conditions specifically and economic conditions
generally.
